<title>JAPAN: Japan electronics shares fall on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Japan electronics shares fall on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>High-priced electronic issues fell in Tokyo on Tuesday morning, hit by profit-taking, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0033 GMT, Sony Corp was down 200 yen at 11,800 and TDK Corp was down 200 yen at 10,100.</p>
<p>Rohm Co Ltd had lost 400 to reach 14,300 and Kyocera Corp had dropped 80 yen to stand at 9,910.  </p>
<p>&quot;The downside of the yen seems limited and the weight of Japanese high-tech stocks is almost at the upper limit in portfolios, which means there is not much room for growth,&quot; a market analyst at a foreign brokerage said.</p>
<p>&quot;The outlook of the stock market is cloudy and investors are hurrying to pocket profits,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
